WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:06.286
Ivy squeezed through the crowd on the porch outside the lodge.

2
00:00:06.287 --> 00:00:09.042
Lunch had just ended.

3
00:00:09.043 --> 00:00:13.151
Now all the campers were checking their mailboxes.

4
00:00:13.152 --> 00:00:17.302
"This is the best time of the day," Ivy thought.

5
00:00:17.303 --> 00:00:21.986
In fact, it was the only time of the day that she liked at camp.

6
00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:25.421
She grabbed an envelope from her mailbox.

7
00:00:25.422 --> 00:00:29.123
"It's from my aunt Lydia. She's awesome.

8
00:00:29.124 --> 00:00:33.521
She understands me better than my parents do."

9
00:00:33.522 --> 00:00:35.510
Ezra didn't answer.

10
00:00:35.511 --> 00:00:38.151
He was reading a postcard.

11
00:00:38.152 --> 00:00:40.687
Glen held up a blue slip.

12
00:00:40.688 --> 00:00:45.610
"I got a package from my parents. Let's go get it."

13
00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:51.049
The kids walked to the office.

14
00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:55.872
"I wrote to Aunt Lydia and told her I hate camp," Ivy said.

15
00:00:55.873 --> 00:01:00.722
"I asked her to rescue me. Maybe she's on her way."

16
00:01:00.723 --> 00:01:03.072
Ivy read the letter.

17
00:01:03.073 --> 00:01:09.797
"Oh, great. Aunt Lydia is at a photography workshop!

18
00:01:09.798 --> 00:01:12.627
She's not coming."

19
00:01:12.628 --> 00:01:16.164
She crumpled the letter and tossed it in a trashcan.

20
00:01:16.165 --> 00:01:18.968
"I guess I'm stuck here."

21
00:01:18.969 --> 00:01:22.972
"I don't believe it!" Ezra said.

22
00:01:22.973 --> 00:01:25.799
"Me neither," Ivy said.

23
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:32.042
"I'm talking about this postcard." Ezra showed it to Glen and Ivy.

24
00:01:32.043 --> 00:01:34.839
"My parents are at the beach!

25
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:40.038
They went on vacation—without me!"

26
00:01:40.039 --> 00:01:43.773
"That looks like a fancy resort," Glen said.

27
00:01:43.774 --> 00:01:47.392
"They're probably having lots of fun."

28
00:01:47.393 --> 00:01:54.615
"Of course they're having fun," Ezra said. "Without me!"

29
00:01:54.616 --> 00:01:57.066
"Don't worry," Glen said.

30
00:01:57.067 --> 00:02:01.355
"Whatever I got from my parents, I'll share with you."

31
00:02:01.356 --> 00:02:05.032
The friends walked into the office.

32
00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:09.633
Glen gave the slip to Mrs. Matsak, the camp secretary.

33
00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:12.575
She handed Glen a box.

34
00:02:12.576 --> 00:02:17.423
"It's already opened," Ivy said, surprised.

35
00:02:17.424 --> 00:02:23.213
Mrs. Matsak rolled her eyes. "Private checks all the packages.

36
00:02:23.214 --> 00:02:28.128
She wants to make sure nobody is getting anything that breaks the rules."

37
00:02:28.129 --> 00:02:32.387
"Wow, look!" Glen showed them the box.

38
00:02:32.388 --> 00:02:36.717
It was full of homemade brownies, candy, and gum! "You

39
00:02:36.718 --> 00:02:43.163
can have one treat now, but the rest stays here," Mrs. Matsak said. "No

40
00:02:43.164 --> 00:02:49.464
food in the cabins. It attracts ants and wild animals." Glen

41
00:02:49.465 --> 00:02:54.609
sighed. "Okay." They

42
00:02:54.610 --> 00:03:01.350
each took a brownie. A

43
00:03:01.351 --> 00:03:06.914
deliveryman came in, sweating as he pushed a handcart. On

44
00:03:06.915 --> 00:03:10.845
it was a statue of a tall bear carved from wood. "Where

45
00:03:10.846 --> 00:03:13.523
should I put this?" "Wonderful!

46
00:03:13.524 --> 00:03:18.280
It's here," Mrs. Matsak said. "Put

47
00:03:18.281 --> 00:03:25.755
it in that corner. Soon it will be placed in the square." "Too

48
00:03:25.756 --> 00:03:29.414
bad it's not a real bear," Ivy whispered. "They'd

49
00:03:29.415 --> 00:03:33.644
have to close camp and send everyone home!" Glen

50
00:03:33.645 --> 00:03:36.520
glanced at Mrs. Matsak. She

51
00:03:36.521 --> 00:03:40.182
was still talking to the deliveryman. "Psst!

52
00:03:40.183 --> 00:03:44.723
Grab some candy from my box!" Ezra

53
00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:49.716
looked nervous. "Uh . . ." "Quick!"

54
00:03:49.717 --> 00:03:52.818
Glen said. Ivy

55
00:03:52.819 --> 00:03:55.620
was already stuffing her pockets. So

56
00:03:55.621 --> 00:04:00.335
was Glen. Ezra took a few pieces. "Thanks,

57
00:04:00.336 --> 00:04:03.576
Mrs. Matsak!" Glen said. As

58
00:04:03.577 --> 00:04:08.603
they left the office, even Ezra was giggling. ***

59
00:04:08.604 --> 00:04:14.023
That night, after evening assembly, the kids walked to the cabins.

60
00:04:14.024 --> 00:04:16.282
Ivy scratched her arm.

61
00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:22.725
"Ugh! More mosquito bites. I hate this stupid camp!"

62
00:04:22.726 --> 00:04:30.461
Ezra frowned. "You know where there aren't any mosquitos? The beach!"

63
00:04:30.462 --> 00:04:35.504
"Cheer up," Glen said. "I'll give you more candy.

64
00:04:35.505 --> 00:04:39.087
I promised to give some to Buck, Huck, and Chuck too.

65
00:04:39.088 --> 00:04:41.607
They're coming to our cabin for it."

66
00:04:41.608 --> 00:04:46.679
"You're giving candy to the Ucks? Why?" Ivy asked.

67
00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.272
"You should keep it for us."

68
00:04:49.273 --> 00:04:54.412
"Yeah, the Ucks are kind of mean," Ezra said.

69
00:04:54.413 --> 00:05:01.253
Glen smiled. "Giving away candy will make me the most popular guy at camp!"

70
00:05:01.254 --> 00:05:03.954
They got to the boys' cabin.

71
00:05:03.955 --> 00:05:06.869
"Whoa!" Glen cried.

72
00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:14.502
Ivy gasped. The door screen was torn open!

73
00:05:14.503 --> 00:05:18.053
Glen slowly opened the door.

74
00:05:18.054 --> 00:05:24.932
Inside, empty candy wrappers littered the floor!

